## Notes for the reviewer

- The writer had no shell; every selector and timing comes from reading `src/runtime/layer.ts`, `scheduler.ts`, `triggers.ts`, `main.ts`, `layer-timing.ts`, `CommandDock.ts`, `BuildWindow.ts`, `PendingOutline.ts`, `src/styles/build-layer.css`, `build-pending.css`, `src/layouts/Base.astro` and `src/sections/projects.build.ts`.
- AC-1 3.2 s: `offset + t(closing) + t(done)` where `offset` is the hero clock already run when the clock was paused (published progress times the duration, at most 200 ms by `startPaused`) and `t` is the stepped clock time of `untilFrames` (20 ms frames). Expected total about 3100 plus up to 37 ms of frame quantization and 16 ms of rounding, against the 3200 ms limit.
- AC-2 boundary: About's top is placed 24 px either side of 75 % of the 800 px viewport (rootMargin `-25%` bottom). The "scrolled up and down" tests place About 24 px past the line so the section after it (a whole About height lower) does not trigger.
- AC-11: the relay card is `cards[0]` of the Projects timeline (asserted by its call); the sample is 60 ms after the second card starts (live after 150 ms), so the relay card is created and the third and fourth are hidden; the click is a real `page.mouse.click` followed by `waitForURL`, which works under the fake clock like the window bar clicks of controls-skip.spec.ts.
- AC-15 bound: a MutationObserver installed by an init script (after the clock's own) records `performance.now()` when `data-build-mode` becomes `pending` and when it is removed; the difference must be at most 3050 ms. `pauseAt(1500)` after `goto` has the same precondition as runtime-fallbacks.spec.ts:39 (under 1.5 s of real time since install).
- layout-invariance compares with a JavaScript-disabled page, not the reduced-motion page of the earlier specs; the reference list includes `.sp-stack` groups and excludes the nav (it slides in). The "after the build" moment uses Shift + Esc (all sections final, dock `done`), not a full 1x walk.
- axe-build-matrix: each cell is its own page; the build is frozen with the hidden-tab trick of effects-axe.spec.ts. The boot cell asserts one `.sp-boot` before the freeze; the done cell asserts the dock state `done`.
