- tests/e2e/behavior-gaps.spec.ts (AC-2, "About starts when its top crosses 75 % ..."): the assertion `expect(l.windows).toBe(0)` taken when the dock log `Reading about.md...` shows was wrong. The window opens at the same instant the log appears (compiler `commandEnd` and layer-timing `commandEnterAt` are the same expression), and PRD AC-2 does not require zero windows then. It is replaced with `windows <= 1` and, when one window exists, `file === 'about.md'`. The 75 % boundary assertions (24 px either side of the line) and the never-two-windows loop are unchanged. Not a weakening: the dropped property was never in the AC, and the new check is the AC's own about.md window requirement at that moment.
- tests/e2e/support/layer.ts:startPaused (ledger row above, still EXISTING_TEST_UPDATED): simplified to the pause-right-after-goto fix. The reload-retry loop, the late-start check, `MAX_START_OFFSET_MS` and `START_ATTEMPTS` are removed. The reviewer's note was right that the retry was unreachable in practice: once `pauseAt(60000)` ran, the clock is paused at 60000, a second `pauseAt` to the same time on a reloaded page cannot rewind it, so the retry would throw rather than recover, and a reload on a paused clock yields no later hero. The return value (hero duration) and all callers are unchanged. The ledger's justification for the original flake cause still holds; its sentence describing the retry/ceiling is superseded by this revision. Note: the writer had no shell and could not grep for other importers of `MAX_START_OFFSET_MS`; the reviewer's `tsc`/lint run will surface any.
